hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1315","Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, and Salam bin Junada narrated to us, and Waki’ both narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “scratched a slug in the qibla of the mosque.” Abu Kurayb said: “It was scratched by spit, sputum, or mucus from the qiblah.”"
